  m_text: 'A shader is a program the graphics card runs for every vertex and every pixel of an object. In Unity it is a file in the project, like these .shader files.


    To use one: create a material (Assets > Create > Material) and choose the shader in its Shader menu, for example Liminal > Water. The shader''s properties become the material''s fields: tune them, then drag the material onto an object.


    Each shader in this scene reads something that the Lit shader does not use. Shader Graph builds the same kind of shaders from nodes; it comes later.'
